<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaninë</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kanina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaninë is a village and medieval castle on a hill above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Vlorë</a> in south-western Albania. The fortress, with late antique origins, guarded the port of Vlorë and was held in turn by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, the Serbian Empire, the lords of Valona and, from 1417, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. Its walls survive as ruins.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanine.jpg" alt="Kaninë" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Decius · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanina_neue_Moschee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
